            type: "paragraph",
            text: "Children can learn these expectations through observation, jokes, peer pressure, media messages, social institutions, and how adults respond to conflict. However, seeing violence in childhood does not mean a person will inevitably become violent. It indicates a possible risk that supportive relationships, education and intervention can help address [2,4].",
